details.image_prompt:
[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two plates centered in the frame with generous negative space, presented at a 3/4 overhead angle of 40 degrees, ensuring every component is clearly identifiable. Shallow depth of field keeps the foreground plate sharp while the second plate behind is softly blurred. Soft natural side light enters from the left, casting gentle shadows and highlighting the sheen of lime juice and olive oil. The setting is a rustic aged oak table with visible wood grain and small crumbs. Props include a rumpled linen napkin tucked under a plate, a discarded lime half, and a small, rustic ceramic ramekin containing extra black beans. The dish consists of two warm, toasted corn tortillas per plate, overflowing with tender, golden-brown flaked cod seasoned with vibrant red chili powder. Beside the fish, a generous scoop of deep-purple red cabbage slaw mixed with creamy, mashed avocado and bright green cilantro creates a colorful contrast. A small serving of earthy black beans sits in a distinct pile on the plate, separated from the tacos. Surfaces show authentic textures: the cod is opaque and flaky with charred spice edges, while the avocado-slaw is creamy and bright. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene captures the moment after cooking, with a few stray cilantro leaves on the table and a small, natural sauce drip on the plate rim. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No plastic sheen, no perfect symmetry, no text, no hands, no logos. The image is indistinguishable from a professional cookbook photograph."
]
